WEBVTT

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:06.742
Spark becomes useful when data and computation benefit from being divided across workers.

00:00:06.742 --> 00:00:12.662
Large file-based transformations, broad scans, batch feature preparation,

00:00:12.662 --> 00:00:18.037
and analytical pipelines across different storage systems are common examples.

00:00:18.037 --> 00:00:26.552
The main benefit is parallelism, but parallelism also introduces new costs such as coordination and shuffling.

00:00:26.552 --> 00:00:30.272
Spark distributes work across multiple processes and often multiple machines.

00:00:30.272 --> 00:00:38.812
The driver coordinates the job, while executors perform tasks on partitions of the data.

00:00:38.812 --> 00:00:45.362
This architecture becomes valuable when the data or workload is too large for one machine or when a platform

00:00:45.362 --> 00:00:48.556
needs scalable parallel processing.
